<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Alexander VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1431">1431</a>–<a href="/years/1503">1503</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Rodrigo Borgia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Alexander VI, born Rodrigo Borgia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, was pope from 1492 to 1503. He used papal power to advance his children, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a>, whom he backed in conquering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> as a duchy. His 1493 bulls divided newly found lands between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal, and his reign became a byword for nepotism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-vi.jpg" alt="Pope Alexander VI" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Pedro Berruguete · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Pope_Alexander_VI_Borgia_(Vatican_Museums_-_Musei_Vaticani,_Vatican).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
